<p>Using the 64-bit edition is recommended. As noted above, it can still build 32-bit installers, and does so by default.</p>

<p>To install 64-bit Inno Setup 7 interactively using <tt>winget</tt> use the following command: <tt>winget install --id JRSoftware.InnoSetup.7 -e -s winget -i</tt></p>

<p>Remember to check the <a href="/isfaq.php">Inno Setup FAQ</a> for solutions to common problems. For more Inno Setup-related downloads, see <a href="/is3rdparty.php">Third-Party Files</a>.</p>

<a name="vnext"></a><h3 class="whitebar">Next Release</h3>

<p>For the next release, we are working hard on various enhancements, including:</p>
<ul>
<li>Zstandard (<tt>zstd</tt>) compression, which unpacks much faster than LZMA, so large installations finish sooner.</li>
</ul>

<p>The next release will also bring many Compiler IDE improvements, including:</p>
<ul>
<li>A new Navigator bar to jump to any section or <tt>[Code]</tt> routine.</li>
<li>A new Inspector panel to view and edit directives and parameters without having to remember their exact names, flags, and defaults. In the <tt>[Code]</tt> section, it shows an outline of your declarations.</li>
<li>A new Minimap next to the editor, showing a miniature of your script so you can see where you are and scroll to any part of it.</li>
<li>Smarter autocompletion, which now also suggests names from your own script, such as your tasks, components, and <tt>[Code]</tt> routines.</li>
<li>Now also available in French, Spanish, Italian, Simplified Chinese, Traditional Chinese, and Korean.</li>
</ul>

<p>You can see all finished features which will be included in the next release by viewing the <a href="https://issrc.innosetup.nl/whatsnew.htm">Revision History file in Git</a>.</p>

<a name="v6"></a><h3 class="whitebar">Inno Setup 6</h3>

<p>Inno Setup 6.7 and its predecessors introduced a large number of significant enhancements including:</p>
<ul>
<li>6.7: Added support for <a href="/images/is-welcome-dark-backimage-org-150.png">custom wizard background images</a> and colors.</li>
<li>6.7: Added support for Windows' <a href="/ishelp/index.php?topic=setup_redirectionguard">RedirectionGuard mitigation</a>.</li>
<li>6.7: Added autocomplete support in the <tt>[Setup]</tt> section for directive values with fixed options, such as all <tt>yes</tt>/<tt>no</tt> directives and others like <tt>WizardStyle</tt>.</li>
<li>6.6: Added support for <a href="/images/is-welcome-dark-org-150.png">dark mode</a> and <a href="/images/is-welcome-polarlight-org-150.png">custom styles</a> to Setup and Uninstall.</li>
<li>6.6: Updated the default font to 9-point Segoe UI.</li>
</ul>

<p><a href="/files/is6-whatsnew.htm">What's new in this Inno Setup 6 version?</a></p>

<p><b>Using Inno Setup commercially?</b> Please <a href="/isorder.php">purchase a license</a>. All commercial licenses are perpetual and require a single payment. They include two years of updates, major and minor, or longer for Enterprise licenses if an extended update period is purchased. After this period, your current version will remain licensed and functional as-is.</p>

